---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TrustBadges from '../../components/TrustBadges.astro';

const title = "Tucson AC Maintenance Guide: What to Do Before Summer | D&H";
const description = "The essential AC maintenance checklist for Tucson homeowners. What you can do yourself, what needs a pro, and when to schedule before the heat hits.";
const canonical = "https://dandhac.com/blog/tucson-ac-maintenance-guide";
const publishDate = "March 15, 2025";
const readTime = "6 min read";
const category = "Maintenance";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Tucson AC Maintenance Guide: What to Do Before Summer",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "D&H Air Conditioning & Heating & Plumbing" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "D&H Air Conditioning", "url": "https://dandhac.com" },
  "datePublished": "2025-03-15",
  "mainEntityOfPage": canonical
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={articleSchema}>

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[var(--color-navy)] to-[var(--color-navy-dark)] hero-pattern relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 md:py-20 relative">
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-blue-400 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-200 transition-colors">Home</a>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
        <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-blue-200 transition-colors">Blog</a>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
        <span class="text-blue-200">Maintenance</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
        <span class="bg-green-500/20 text-green-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full">{category}</span>
        <span class="text-blue-300 text-xs">{publishDate}</span>
        <span class="text-blue-400 text-xs">· {readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-white leading-[1.1] mb-5">
        The Tucson AC Maintenance Guide: What to Do Before Summer Hits
      </h1>
      <p class="text-blue-200 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        When you're staring down months of 105°F+ days, your AC isn't optional. Here's what to do in spring to make sure it's ready.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="py-14 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">

        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-8">
          Tucson's AC systems work harder than almost anywhere else in the country. The combination of extreme heat, dry air, and monsoon humidity makes routine maintenance not just smart — it's essential. Here's what to check before the heat arrives.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">What you can do yourself</h2>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-6 mb-3">Replace your air filter</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          In Tucson, you should replace your filter every 30–60 days during peak season — more often than the national recommendation. Desert dust, pollen, and monsoon debris clog filters faster here. A clean filter is the single easiest thing you can do to extend your system's life.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-6 mb-3">Clear the area around your outdoor condenser</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Your outdoor condenser needs clear airflow on all sides. Trim back any shrubs or plants to at least 18 inches from the unit. Remove any debris that collected over winter. Don't cover the unit.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-6 mb-3">Test your thermostat</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Switch to Cool mode and drop the temperature below the current room temperature. The system should kick on within a minute or two. If it doesn't — or if it runs but doesn't cool — you've got a starting problem to address before summer.
        </p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-6 mb-3">Check and clear the condensate drain</h3>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Your AC removes humidity from the air and drains it outside. If the condensate drain line clogs, water backs up and can damage your system or cause water damage in your home. Locate the drain line (usually a PVC pipe near the air handler) and flush it with a cup of diluted bleach once a season.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">What needs a professional</h2>

        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          The DIY steps above are important, but they won't catch everything. A professional tune-up covers the things that need testing equipment and trained eyes:
        </p>

        <ul class="space-y-3 mb-8">
          {[
            'Refrigerant level check and leak testing',
            'Electrical connection inspection and tightening',
            'Capacitor and contactor testing',
            'Evaporator and condenser coil cleaning',
            'Airflow measurement and duct inspection',
            'Thermostat calibration',
            'Safety control testing',
          ].map(item => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3 text-[var(--color-muted)] text-base">
              <svg class="shrink-0 mt-1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-success)" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
              {item}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">When to schedule</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Schedule your tune-up in March or April — before the heat hits and before every other homeowner in Tucson is calling at the same time. By May, wait times stretch out. By June, you're competing for emergency slots. Spring is the time.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-orange-50 border border-orange-200 rounded-2xl p-6 my-10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mb-2">The Family Maintenance Plan</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-sm leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For $199/year per system, D&H's Family Maintenance Plan covers two tune-ups (spring and fall), priority dispatch in emergencies, 10% off all repairs, and no after-hours surcharges.
          </p>
          <a href="/family-maintenance-plan" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--color-navy)] font-bold text-sm hover:text-[var(--color-orange)] transition-colors">
            See plan details →
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <TrustBadges />

  <section class="bg-[var(--color-navy)] py-14">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl text-white mb-4">Ready for a tune-up?</h2>
      <p class="text-blue-200 text-lg mb-8">Book before summer — slots fill up fast.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-[var(--color-orange)] hover:bg-[var(--color-orange-dark)] text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition-colors shadow-lg">
          Schedule a Tune-Up
        </a>
        <a href="/family-maintenance-plan" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border-2 border-white text-white hover:bg-white hover:text-[var(--color-navy)] font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition-colors">
          See Maintenance Plan
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
